  "id": "Compound::DB01115 - Gene::1544",
  "verbalization": "Nifedipine, a calcium channel blocker, is linked to Cyp1a2 through a series of molecular and metabolic pathways. The evidence suggests that Nifedipine, as part of the Dihydropyridine class, binds to Cyp1a2, which is involved in the oxidation of quinone or similar compounds. This connection is further supported by the involvement of Cyp2c9, a cytochrome P450 enzyme, in the metabolic activation of Cyp1a2. The shared pathway involves the metabolic processing of quinone-like substrates, which is a common mechanism in the activation of cytochrome P450 enzymes. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Nifedipine influences Cyp1a2 activity, likely through its role in modulating the metabolic profile of the drug. The evidence underscores a dependency on the metabolic pathways that are central to the activation of Cyp1a2, suggesting a direct or indirect interaction that is consistent with the observed biological effects.",
